<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - a comment ABOVE the root breaks
        `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading parent-xml error.

        Acquisitions gap-fix, Item 6.2/6.4 (2026-08-31, agent-output/design-requirements.md §2
        ITEM 6, §0.5 Q9). 🔴 NAMED First_Submission_DateTime__c, NOT ..._Date__c, on purpose -
        DateTime per ARCHITECTURE.md §1's suffix-discipline rule. The source value,
        Lead.First_Seen_Date__c, is ITSELF a DateTime despite its Date suffix (a recorded
        pre-existing ARCHITECTURE.md violation LeadConvertService documents and refuses to rename
        because that would mean delete-and-recreate). This field does not repeat that mistake:
        it is a straight MIN(Lead.First_Seen_Date__c) GROUP BY ConvertedContactId, so a DateTime
        target lets the instant map across with no `.date()` truncation.

        🔴 READ Deals_Lost__c.field-meta.xml's header (this same folder) for the full
        metric-inversion warning - it applies here identically. This field covers only brokers
        who have a Contact (Lead converted); brokerLeaderboard remains authoritative for "first
        submission" across the WHOLE broker population, winners and losers, Contact or not.

        THE JOIN IS Lead.ConvertedContactId - NOT Lead.Broker_First__c, which is a Text(255)
        mirror of the brokerage FIRM NAME (BrokerPortalService sets it identically to
        input.brokerageFirm) and carries no broker-identity link at all. Maintained nightly by
        BrokerCounterRecalcBatch, batched over Contact, system mode. READ-ONLY in every
        user-facing permission set; DPEG_Admin_Access carries an editable grant matching this
        org's established pattern for batch-maintained fields whose test fixtures may set them
        directly (see Deals_Lost__c's header for the RunLocalTests reasoning).
    -->
    <fullName>First_Submission_DateTime__c</fullName>
    <description>Earliest Lead.First_Seen_Date__c (itself a DateTime) among Leads converted to this Contact, i.e. this broker's first-ever submission DPEG has record of. Covers ONLY brokers who have a Contact (Lead converted) - see Deals_Lost__c for the full population caveat. Authoritative population: brokerLeaderboard / BrokerLeaderboardService. Maintained nightly by BrokerCounterRecalcBatch.</description>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <label>First Submission DateTime</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>DateTime</type>
</CustomField>
